From 35909e6ae55fdfbde03c449a0ca170dda6bbbd3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Brian C. Lane" <bcl@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:54:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] tests: t3000-resize-fs.sh mount fails

Running the test suite on Fedora 45 and the mount after making the fat32
filesystem fails with:

mount /dev/sdb1 /root/parted/tests/gt-t3000-resize-fs.sh.zUu3/mnt
mount: /root/parted/tests/gt-t3000-resize-fs.sh.zUu3/mnt: wrong fs type, bad option, bad superblock on /dev/sdb1, missing codepage or helper program, or other error.
       dmesg(1) may have more information after failed mount system call.

Adding a call to wait_for_dev_to_appear_ fixes it so that it
consistently passes. I could not see it remove the partition, either in
udev event monitoring, or adding debugging to the test script, but it
consistently fails without waiting.
---
 tests/t3000-resize-fs.sh | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/t3000-resize-fs.sh b/tests/t3000-resize-fs.sh
index 00518422..33703da3 100755
--- a/tests/t3000-resize-fs.sh
+++ b/tests/t3000-resize-fs.sh
@@ -86,6 +86,9 @@ for fs_type in $FSTYPES; do
   # create the file system
   $mkfs_cmd ${dev}1 || fail=1
 
+  # Make sure the partition is there
+  wait_for_dev_to_appear_ ${dev}1
+
   # create 500 deep directory tree with longest name 4000 characters
   # to catch core dump in libparted/fs/r/fat/count.c flag_traverse_dir()
   # overflowing 512 byte file_name local buffer.
